# elohim/elohim-views — the wire contract

What belongs here: View and InputView types with `#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]` and
`#[derive(TS)]`, matching their view schemas in `elohim/sdk/schemas/v1/views/`. The TypeScript
projection is generated (`cargo test export_bindings` writes
`elohim/sdk/storage-client-ts/src/generated/`) and never hand-edited.

Two traps are structural, not edit-time. ts-rs derives import paths from the source crate's
location, so a View type moves between crates only in one atomic migration with a sha256 diff of
the generated TypeScript. And `deny.toml` keeps every consumer except the server-side wrappers on
this crate rather than on `elohim-storage`. The schema-contract harness and the codegen freshness
check hold both, so `covers: subtree` carries no rule.
